Formalizing the Connectivity Theorem for the Matrix Multiplication Flip Graph in ACL2
Quan Luu, Zeke Medley, Panagiotis Manolios (ACL2 Workshop 2026)

Supporting materials for the paper: an ACL2 proof that the flip graph of
matrix multiplication schemes over F2 is strongly connected under flip and
plus transformations (Theorem 4.1 of Medley, Gokul, Luu and Manolios,
"GPU-Accelerated Search for Fast Matrix Multiplication over F2", ALENEX 2027).
The main theorem is flip-plus-connectivity in main.lisp.

Certification
-------------
From this directory, with ACL2 built and the community books available:

  cert.pl -j 4 overview-proof.lisp

certifies every book (overview-proof includes overview-prelims, which
includes main, which includes the rest).  The development was certified with
a development snapshot of ACL2 8.7 (git 98c07036d7, 2026-09-01) on SBCL 2.6.4
(macOS, Apple Silicon); certifying everything from scratch takes about one
minute with four parallel jobs.  It uses no trust tags, skip-proofs or defaxiom, and
depends only on std (util/define, util/defrule, obags, lists, basic),
kestrel/bv (bitand, bitxor) and arithmetic/top-with-meta from the community
books.

Where to start
--------------
overview-prelims.lisp and overview-proof.lisp are a commented tour of the
development: every definition and theorem discussed in the paper, restated
verbatim from the books below with proof hints and routine typing theorems
left out.  Because ACL2 accepts a restated event only if it is identical to
the original, certifying the two files checks that the tour agrees with the
development.  Read overview-prelims.lisp first.

Books
-----
bits.lisp           bit lists and bit matrices over F2
bags.lisp           lemmas about ordered bags (std/obags) used for schemes
scheme.lisp         summands, schemes, flip and plus, moves and paths
tensor.lisp         tensors of summands and schemes
preservation.lisp   valid paths preserve the scheme sum
mm-tensor.lisp      the matrix multiplication tensor
mmt.lisp            lemma:mmt, the entry law of mm-tensor
span.lisp           lemma:span, the spanning lemma
add-duplicate.lisp  lemma:add-duplicate-sum, adding a duplicate sum
paths.lisp          composing paths; deleting an identical pair
entry.lisp          entry lemmas for the operations on bit lists
iterate.lisp        walking a chain of duplicate-sum steps (grow-chain)
gf2span.lisp        the F2 span layer: in-spanp, span-witness, bases
arbitrary.lisp      the A, B and C legs of adding an arbitrary summand
add-arbitrary.lisp  lem:add-arbitrary, adding an arbitrary summand
parity.lisp         unit summands and the even-multiplicity argument
zero-support.lisp   decomposing summands into unit summands
zero-subset.lisp    lemma:zero-subset, deleting a zero-summing submultiset
main.lisp           thm:main, flip-plus-connectivity
overview-prelims.lisp, overview-proof.lisp   the commented tour (see above)
